{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00042", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It impersonates a financial institution (\"NavyFed\") and reports a suspicious transaction (\"$870 withdrawn at ATMSW-2\"). Crucially, it directs the recipient to a shortened, suspicious link (`bit.ly/navyauth`) to \"dispute\" the transaction, which is a common tactic used by phishers to steal credentials or personal information. The tone creates a sense of urgency regarding a financial loss.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
