{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00099", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The URL provided, `https://irs.gov.secure-fundhub.com`, is highly suspicious. While it attempts to mimic the official IRS domain (`irs.gov`), the addition of `-fundhub.com` makes it a clear attempt at domain spoofing or phishing. The message creates a sense of urgency (\"immediately to ensure precise payment\") and implies a financial requirement, which are classic tactics used in phishing scams.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00100", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It uses brand impersonation by referencing \"UNILEVER PLC,\" which is a common tactic in phishing to gain trust. The message presents an overly attractive offer (\"Earn 500 bucks every week\") which is a classic lure used in scams. Most critically, it directs the recipient to a suspicious, non-official-looking URL (`https://unileverplcpromo01.wixsite.com/wrap`). Legitimate corporate recruitment or promotional offers would typically direct users to the official company website, not a generic, newly created Wix site.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
