{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00241", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. The message uses sensational, clickbait-style language (\"RACIST outburst captured on video camera\") to entice the recipient into clicking the provided link. The URL, `http://supplyform.boutique/YEXP11Qs`, is highly suspicious. It uses a generic-sounding domain (`boutique`) combined with a non-standard path, which is a common tactic used in phishing attempts to host malicious content or credential harvesting forms. There is no context suggesting this is a legitimate news alert from a reputable source.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00242", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several characteristics of a potential scam, although it lacks the typical high-pressure tactics of classic smishing. The language is overly sentimental, vague, and immediately attempts to establish a personal, intimate connection (\"you are a kind person,\" \"this is fate\"). This is a common tactic used in romance scams, which often begin via unsolicited messages like this. The lack of any legitimate context (e.g., a bank alert, delivery notification) combined with the sudden, intense personal approach is highly suspicious. While it doesn't contain a suspicious link or an immediate request for money, the intent appears to be social engineering to build trust for a future malicious purpose.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
