{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00361", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message consists only of a shortened, suspicious-looking URL. There is no accompanying text to provide context, but the presence of an unsolicited, obfuscated link is a major red flag. Shortened or unusual URLs are frequently used in smishing attacks to hide the true destination of the link, which often leads to phishing pages designed to steal credentials or install malware. The lack of any legitimate context or sender identification strongly suggests malicious intent.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
