{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00497", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It impersonates a legitimate entity (U.S.P.S.), creates a sense of urgency/problem (\"cannot be delivered due to incomplete address information\"), and directs the recipient to a suspicious, non-official-looking link (`https://uuhups.com`). The request is to click a link to \"confirm\" personal information (address), which is a common tactic in phishing attacks.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00499", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It uses a sense of urgency (\"if this wasn't you\") related to a specific, large financial transaction ($1,989.50 Charge on E-Bay). Crucially, it directs the recipient to click a suspicious, non-official-looking URL (`mastermulticentro.com/ss`) to take action (DENY). This combination of financial threat, urgency, and a suspicious link is characteristic of phishing attempts designed to steal credentials or personal information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00500", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several classic indicators of smishing. It impersonates a legitimate financial institution (Bank of America - BOFA) and creates a sense of urgency (\"kindly contact us... now\") regarding a potentially fraudulent transaction. The message prompts the recipient to take immediate action by calling a provided phone number, which is a common tactic used by scammers to trick victims into revealing personal information or authorizing payments.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
