{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00516", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message appears to be a casual conversation or a piece of advice regarding shipping options, discussing delivery times and potential customs issues (\"bribe nipost\"). There are no indicators of phishing, such as urgent demands, suspicious links, requests for personal information, or impersonation of a known brand. The language is informal and conversational.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00518", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message \"I've sent ü my part..\" is very brief and lacks any overt indicators of smishing, such as urgent demands, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. The use of \"ü\" instead of \"you\" is a minor stylistic choice, but the overall content suggests a casual, informal communication between known parties, likely related to a shared task or agreement. Therefore, it appears to be a legitimate, informal message.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
