{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00528", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It creates a sense of urgency (\"Your package cannot be delivered\") to prompt immediate action. Crucially, it contains a suspicious link (`https://usp-snavn.top`). The domain name appears non-standard and is likely designed to mimic a legitimate shipping or delivery service, which is a common tactic in phishing attacks. The request is to \"fill in the correct address online,\" which is a pretext to harvest personal information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00529", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It impersonates a well-known brand (Netflix) to create a sense of urgency (\"placed on hold,\" \"as soon as possible\") regarding a service interruption. It then directs the recipient to click a suspicious, non-official-looking URL (`http://s957290943.onlinehome.us/`) to \"update billing information,\" which is a classic tactic for harvesting sensitive personal and financial data.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00530", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. The text uses deliberate misspellings and abbreviations (\"You.r,\" \"paymen.t,\" \"Septemb.er,\" \"o.ur,\" \"pre.sent\") which is a common tactic to bypass basic spam filters. More critically, it includes a suspicious, shortened, and non-standard URL (`f4RSX.COM/8vxyyUpY4d`) immediately following a notification about a payment, suggesting the link is intended to lead the recipient to a malicious site, likely to steal credentials or personal information under the guise of a \"present.\" The combination of an unsolicited payment confirmation followed by a suspicious link is highly indicative of a phishing attempt.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00531", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The use of \"Last reminder!\" and \"You got 12h left!\" creates a high sense of urgency, a common tactic in phishing to pressure the recipient into acting without thinking. Furthermore, the link provided, `twistedcapsule.com/dRBILnD`, uses a non-standard, suspicious domain name that is likely not associated with a legitimate giveaway or Apple. The message also impersonates a prize notification (\"iPad Pro you won from August Giveaway\"), which is a classic social engineering lure.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00533", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It impersonates a legitimate entity (USPS) and creates a sense of urgency/problem (\"could not be delivered due to incomplete address information\"). Crucially, it directs the recipient to click a suspicious, non-official-looking link (`usps.myservice-tracking.com`) to resolve the issue, which is a classic phishing tactic designed to steal personal information or credentials. The unusual instructions regarding replying 'Y' and then re-opening the text message further suggest a manipulative or malicious process.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
