{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00598", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message appears to be a notification regarding an order tracking service, which is a common function of legitimate e-commerce or shipping platforms. The link provided, `https://link.aftership.com/3SeJ6`, uses the domain `aftership.com`, which is a known and legitimate service for order tracking. There are no immediate signs of high-pressure urgency, requests for sensitive personal information (like passwords or credit card numbers), or obvious typos/malicious redirects that would strongly suggest a phishing attempt. While any link can potentially be malicious, based on the context and the recognizable brand/service name, it leans towards being legitimate.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
