{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00618", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message is very short and contains only a refusal (\"No. I dont want to hear anything\"). There are no suspicious cues present such as urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. The message is too brief to establish a clear context, but the lack of any malicious indicators strongly suggests it is not a phishing attempt. It reads more like a direct, albeit abrupt, response to a previous communication.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
