{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00648", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing (or more accurately, spam/scam, but fitting the phishing category due to the malicious intent). The primary evidence is the unsolicited, sexually suggestive nature of the message (\"HotJackie871 is hoping for intimate pleasures\") combined with a suspicious, non-standard URL (`http://tftjrl.com/8xGFWIB`). This combination is designed to lure the recipient into clicking a link, likely to a malicious or inappropriate website. There is no legitimate context for this message.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00649", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message contains highly informal, colloquial language (\"brothas\") and a suggestive, playful tone (\"princess\"). There are no indicators of urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. The content appears to be part of a casual, personal conversation.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00650", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing or a similar type of unsolicited scam. The request to \"rate or like the hotel we booked\" is vague and unsolicited, suggesting a potential survey scam or a pretext to gain contact information. The inclusion of a specific WhatsApp number and the arbitrary restriction (\"under 20 years old not allowed\") are common tactics used in phishing attempts to create a sense of exclusivity or urgency, prompting the recipient to engage with the provided contact method. There is no clear, legitimate context provided for why the recipient is being asked to participate in this rating scheme.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00651", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. The message uses vague, enticing language (\"The Natural Path to Deeper Sleep\") which is a common tactic to lure users into clicking. More critically, it contains a shortened, suspicious URL (`http://abundantbis.limited/x7iLqJ`). The domain name (`abundantbis.limited`) does not appear to belong to a known, reputable health or sleep organization, and the use of a URL shortener/obscured domain is a major red flag for phishing attempts designed to hide the true destination of the link. There is no context provided to suggest this message is legitimate.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00652", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message is classified as ham. The message is very informal, uses abbreviations (\"ü\" for you, \"C\" for can/to), and appears to be a casual, conversational query between people who know each other. There are no indicators of smishing, such as urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00654", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It uses a sense of urgency (\"security alert,\" \"fraudulent withdrawal\") to prompt immediate action. It impersonates a known entity (\"OnPoint\") to gain trust. Most critically, it includes a suspicious, non-official-looking link (`https://jenshade.com/onpoint/on/org`) which is designed to trick the recipient into entering sensitive information or clicking malware.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00655", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several suspicious cues indicative of smishing. The message uses a shortened, non-official-looking domain name (\"Oprahstoday.com\") which is a common tactic for phishing. It promotes a \"giveaway\" and a \"Discount,\" which creates a sense of opportunity and urgency, pressuring the recipient to click the link. The structure, including the \"FRM:\" and \"MSG:\" prefixes, is often used in automated or deceptive messaging.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00656", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message appears to be a casual, conversational message, likely a personal communication or a misunderstanding between individuals. There are no indicators of phishing, such as urgent demands, suspicious links, requests for personal information, or brand impersonation. The language is informal and relates to a phone call situation.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00657", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message is classified as ham. The message is a brief, informal communication from someone named \"Hrishi\" asking the recipient not to answer a call because there is something important to discuss. There are no suspicious cues such as urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. It reads like a personal text message.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00659", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. Key suspicious cues include:\n1. **Urgency/Threat:** The message immediately creates a sense of crisis (\"Your Account has been limited,\" \"We have locked your Account ID\").\n2. **Suspicious Link:** The URL provided (`http://s950712130.onlinehome.us`) is highly irregular, does not resemble the official PayPal domain, and uses a generic, suspicious structure.\n3. **Request for Action/Verification:** It demands the user click a link to \"verify your Account\" to resolve the supposed issue, which is a classic phishing tactic.\n4. **Brand Impersonation:** It impersonates \"Paypal service,\" a common tactic used by scammers.\n\nThe combination of urgency, a suspicious link, and impersonation strongly suggests this is a phishing attempt.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00660", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message is classified as ham because it is an informal, casual conversation between people (\"O ic lol. Should play 9 doors sometime yo\"). It contains no suspicious elements such as urgency, links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00662", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The message uses urgent language (\"has been 'I0cked', fix your biIls detalLs-now!\"), which is a common tactic to induce panic and prompt immediate action. It also contains a suspicious, shortened URL (`//_9qr.de/bvb2Bm`) that is not associated with the legitimate Amazon domain, suggesting it is a phishing link designed to steal credentials or personal information. Furthermore, it impersonates a known brand (Amazon) to gain the recipient's trust.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00663", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message \"Hui xin is in da lib\" is very brief and informal. It appears to be a casual update or message between people who know each other, possibly indicating the location of a person named Hui Xin. There are no indicators of urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. The language is colloquial (\"da lib\" instead of \"the library\"), which is consistent with informal personal communication.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00664", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The primary suspicious cues are the unsolicited nature of the message, the promise of unusually high and easy earnings (\"earn $600 -1000 perday\"), and the call to action directing the user to join a group via a link (in this case, a WhatsApp link, which is often used in phishing/scam schemes). The promise of quick, large money is a classic lure used in financial scams.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
