{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00684", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The message impersonates a known financial institution, \"WELLS FARGO,\" which is a common tactic in phishing attacks. It creates a sense of urgency or necessity by stating \"Validation required on your account.\" Most critically, it includes a suspicious, shortened URL (`wowgo.app.link/luAzIC`) that directs the recipient to an external, non-official domain, which is designed to trick the user into entering sensitive information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
