{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00803", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It uses a common brand impersonation (USPS) to create a sense of urgency and concern (\"Your package is being returned to the sender\"). Crucially, it includes a suspicious, shortened link (`https://is.gd/ERR1293`) that directs the recipient to an external site, likely to harvest personal information or payment details under the guise of updating an address. The combination of a service notification, urgency, and a suspicious link is a classic smishing tactic.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
