{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00890", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message exhibits several characteristics of a personal, informal conversation rather than a phishing attempt. The language is highly colloquial (\"cool ta luv,\" \"v.tired,\" \"spk sn x\"), suggesting a close relationship between the sender and recipient. The content discusses a personal event (a social services inspection at a nursery) and expresses fatigue, which is typical of personal communication. There are no suspicious cues such as urgent demands, requests for personal information, links, or brand impersonation.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00891", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. It uses an unsolicited invitation (\"Dear friend\") to join a group promising unusually high, guaranteed returns (\"earn 1000-5000US per day\") in a high-risk area like cryptocurrency. This promise of quick, large wealth is a classic lure used in financial scams. Furthermore, it directs the recipient to click a link to join a group, which is a common vector for phishing or malware distribution, even if the link provided here is to WhatsApp. The overall tone is promotional and highly enticing, designed to bypass critical thinking.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00892", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message contains a link that is highly suspicious. The URL, `http://psjzzw.com/no2hgVq`, is a short, non-standard domain, which is a common tactic used in smishing attacks to hide the true destination of the link. While the initial greeting (\"Hi baby\") suggests a personal context, the unsolicited, suspicious link immediately following the personal greeting is a strong indicator of a phishing attempt, potentially leading to malware download or credential harvesting.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
