{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00950", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. Specifically, it uses brand impersonation by referencing \"Oprah,\" which is a common tactic to lure victims. It also contains a suspicious link (`oprahstoday.com`), which is likely a phishing domain designed to look legitimate but is used to steal information. The message promotes a \"biggest giveaway,\" creating a sense of excitement and urgency to encourage immediate clicking.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
