{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01082", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message contains several suspicious cues indicative of smishing. The sender ID, \"IRS\\_TAX\\_REFUND\\_B2D,\" attempts to impersonate a legitimate government agency (IRS) and suggests a financial incentive (tax refund). The message itself is a direct link to a PDF document, which is a common tactic used in phishing attacks to trick recipients into downloading malware or revealing sensitive information. The combination of impersonation, a financial lure, and an unsolicited document link is highly suspicious.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
