{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01234", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The primary suspicious cue is the request to click a link to resolve a delivery issue, which is a common tactic in phishing. Furthermore, the URL provided, `https://usp-screw.top`, appears highly suspicious. It uses a non-standard, potentially deceptive domain structure (`.top`) and does not resemble the official domain of a major courier service (like UPS, which is often impersonated). The message creates a sense of urgency (\"cannot be delivered\") to prompt immediate action from the recipient.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
