{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01236", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It uses brand impersonation by referencing \"Wells Fargo Bank.\" It creates a sense of urgency and fear (\"Account is suspended due to recent database breach for safety\"). Most critically, it includes a suspicious link (`https://poiasj5.cf/wellsfargo.com/?restore`) which does not appear to be an official Wells Fargo domain, suggesting a phishing attempt to steal credentials or personal information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
