{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01357", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message appears to be a casual, conversational exchange rather than a malicious attempt to trick the recipient. There are no indicators of urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. The language is informal (\"Hmmm...k...but i want to change the field quickly da:-)i wanna get system administrator or network administrator..\"), suggesting a discussion about career goals or job roles between known parties.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01358", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. The initial statement, \"Your bill is paid for March,\" might be a pretext to establish a sense of legitimacy or context. However, the immediate follow-up with an unsolicited \"little gift\" and a shortened, suspicious-looking URL (`catererhunger.com/Okk7d5ha2y`) is highly indicative of a phishing attempt. Legitimate companies rarely send unsolicited \"gifts\" via SMS that require clicking an unknown link. The URL itself is not associated with a known, trusted service.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01360", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message is classified as ham. The message is a casual, informal text exchange (\"Hey tmr maybe can meet you at yck\"). It contains no elements of urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. It appears to be an ordinary conversation between acquaintances.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
