{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01362", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message is classified as ham. The content is a casual, conversational exchange (\"Ok then i'll let him noe later n ask him call u tmr...\"). It contains no indicators of phishing, such as urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. It reads like a normal text message between acquaintances.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01363", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It creates a sense of urgency (\"as soon as possible,\" \"having some trouble with your current billing information\") to prompt immediate action. It impersonates a well-known brand (\"The Netflix team\"). Most critically, it includes a suspicious, non-official-looking link (`https://gotommbr.myclickfunnels.com/`) that directs the user to an external site, which is a classic tactic used in phishing attacks to steal credentials or payment information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01364", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. The use of an informal, slightly unprofessional greeting (\"(:) Hey\") combined with an unsolicited notification about a \"contest\" is a common tactic used in phishing attempts. The request to reply with \"Ok\" is a low-effort way to engage the recipient and potentially lead to further malicious communication or data harvesting. The misspelling of \"superiel\" (likely intended as \"super prize\" or similar) is another red flag indicating a lack of professional vetting, typical of spam or phishing campaigns. There is no clear context or legitimate reason for this message to be sent.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01365", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message contains informal language, abbreviations (\"noe,\" \"da,\" \"c lar\"), and appears to be a casual, personal conversation between individuals. There are no indicators of urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. Therefore, it is classified as legitimate communication.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01366", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several characteristics that suggest it is not a typical smishing attempt, but rather a personal, informal, and potentially confrontational message. There are no suspicious cues such as urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. The language is highly informal (\"tel u,\" \"k\"), which is consistent with casual texting between known parties. The content itself is vague and conversational, not indicative of a phishing attempt.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01367", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It uses a lure (\"Get $100 Reward\") to entice the recipient, which is a common tactic in phishing. More critically, the link provided, `http://summe.shopping/Hhj0J3`, is highly suspicious. It does not appear to be an official HomeDepot domain, and the use of a generic, non-branded domain combined with a short, random string is characteristic of malicious shorteners or phishing sites designed to mimic legitimate offers. The combination of a financial incentive and a suspicious, non-official link strongly suggests an attempt to steal credentials or personal information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01368", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. It uses a common pretext (delivery issue) to create a sense of urgency or necessity for action. Crucially, it directs the recipient to a link (`https://my-fed-ex.com/`) that is designed to look like an official FedEx domain but is likely a phishing site. While it mentions a known brand (FedEx), the unsolicited nature and the request to click a link to resolve a supposed issue are classic phishing tactics.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01369", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message contains no typical indicators of smishing, such as urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. Instead, it appears to be a fragment of a technical instruction or a math problem explanation, suggesting it is part of a legitimate, ongoing conversation or instruction set.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01370", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It uses brand impersonation (\"Amazon\") to create a sense of legitimacy. It employs a lure (winning a raffle) to entice the recipient. Most critically, it contains a suspicious, non-standard URL (`b2gxv.info/5ssC5f2SEG`) which is characteristic of phishing attempts designed to steal credentials or install malware. The message creates a sense of excitement/urgency associated with a prize.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01371", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message consists solely of a shortened, suspicious-looking URL. There is no accompanying text to provide context, but the presence of an unsolicited, shortened link is a major red flag in SMS communications. Shortened links are frequently used in smishing attacks to obscure the true destination of the link, which often leads to phishing pages designed to steal credentials or install malware. The lack of any legitimate context or sender identification strongly suggests malicious intent.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01372", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message exhibits several characteristics of ham (legitimate/casual conversation) rather than smishing. The language is highly informal, conversational, and uses slang (\"moneY,\" \"aint a thing,\" \"sha!\"). There are no suspicious cues such as urgency, requests for personal information, payment demands, or suspicious links. The content appears to be a casual, friendly check-in.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
