{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01444", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It impersonates a legitimate financial institution (Bank of America - BOfA) and creates a sense of urgency by claiming the account has been locked due to \"unusual activity.\" Crucially, it includes a suspicious, non-official-looking link (`https://api.hubapi.com/...`) that directs the user to click to \"restore\" the account, which is a classic phishing tactic designed to steal credentials or personal information. The inclusion of specific, alarming details like a login from a foreign IP address (Zimbabwe) is designed to panic the recipient into clicking the link immediately.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
