{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01446", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The sender uses a non-standard, potentially spoofed domain (\"NTFLIX.ID\" instead of the official Netflix domain) and employs urgency (\"Renewal-your-bill-now\"). Furthermore, it contains a suspicious, shortened URL (`unusa.id/4mx6`) which is designed to trick the recipient into clicking and entering sensitive information or payment details. The message structure is typical of phishing attempts designed to mimic legitimate service notifications.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01447", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message \"Are you comingdown later?\" is a very casual, conversational message. It lacks any of the typical indicators of smishing, such as urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. It appears to be a simple social inquiry between known parties.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01448", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The message uses an unsolicited, highly urgent tone (\"ready for you NOW!!\") to entice the recipient. It presents a low-cost housing offer, which is a common lure in scams. Most critically, it contains a suspicious, non-standard URL (`approvedlink.info/pvKdPvhsrMpn`) that is designed to look like a legitimate link but is likely malicious, aiming to steal personal information or install malware. There is no context to suggest this is from a legitimate real estate agent or service.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01449", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. Key suspicious cues include:\n1. **Urgency/Problem Creation:** It creates a sense of urgency by claiming a package delivery failure due to incomplete address information.\n2. **Suspicious Link:** The provided URL, `https://uspsikqc.top`, is highly suspicious. It does not use the official USPS domain (`usps.com`) and uses a generic, non-official top-level domain (.top), which is a common tactic in phishing.\n3. **Request for Action/Information:** It directs the user to click a link to \"confirm your address,\" which is a common vector for credential harvesting or malware installation.\n4. **Unusual Instructions:** The instruction to \"reply Y, then exit the text message and open it again to activate the link\" is an unusual and manipulative instruction designed to confuse the user or bypass security checks.\n\nThe combination of brand impersonation (USPS) with a non-official, suspicious link and a request for personal data makes this clearly malicious.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01451", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several characteristics of smishing. It uses a common, somewhat personal opening (\"Michael, are you stressed out?\") to build rapport, which is a tactic often used in phishing. The core of the message is a promotional pitch for CBD, which is a common vector for unsolicited commercial messages. The most significant red flag is the inclusion of a suspicious, shortened URL (`cbdnews2.best/bhUisK72aa`). This URL is not from a recognizable, legitimate health authority or major brand, and the use of a shortened link is designed to obscure the true destination of the link, a hallmark of phishing attempts. Furthermore, while it doesn't explicitly ask for passwords, it directs the recipient to an external, unverified site, which is the goal of smishing—to trick the user into clicking and potentially entering personal or financial information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01452", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message is classified as ham because it is a casual, conversational instruction between two parties. It does not contain any of the typical hallmarks of smishing, such as urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. The context suggests a personal communication rather than a malicious attempt to trick the recipient.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01453", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. The phrase \"Your bill is paid for March\" suggests a financial or service-related context, which is often used in phishing attempts to gain trust. The inclusion of a link, `fritzclosets.com/PV06ExwSdV`, is highly suspicious. The domain name, `fritzclosets.com`, does not appear to be associated with a standard utility or billing service, and the URL structure is designed to look like a tracking or promotional link, which is a common tactic in smishing to direct users to a malicious site. The offer of a \"little gift\" is a common lure used to entice clicks.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01454", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing.\n1. **Brand Impersonation:** It impersonates the United States Postal Service (USPS), a common tactic in phishing.\n2. **Urgency/Action Required:** It creates a sense of urgency (\"Please update it timely\") regarding a package delay.\n3. **Suspicious Link:** The URL provided, `https://www.upotps.com/go/Tracking/G01U6`, is not the official USPS domain (which is typically usps.com). The slight misspelling or variation (`upotps.com`) is a classic phishing technique.\n4. **Request for Information/Action:** It prompts the user to reply with information or click a link to \"reconfirm your address,\" which is a request for personal data.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01455", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing.\n1. **Brand Impersonation:** It impersonates the Internal Revenue Service (IRS), a common tactic in phishing attacks.\n2. **Urgency and Threat:** It creates a sense of urgency (\"immediately,\" \"avoid potential delays or penalties\") and implies a financial benefit (tax refund) contingent on immediate action.\n3. **Suspicious Link:** The provided URL, `https://irs.gov.secure-fundhub.com`, is highly suspicious. While it contains \"irs.gov,\" the actual domain is `secure-fundhub.com`, which is not the official IRS domain (`irs.gov`). This is a classic example of a deceptive URL structure.\n4. **Request for Personal Information:** It explicitly asks the recipient to \"confirm your information\" via the link, which is a request for sensitive personal data.\n\nThese cues strongly suggest an attempt to trick the user into providing personal information or clicking a malicious link.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01457", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message exhibits several characteristics of informal, personal communication rather than a malicious attempt at phishing. There is no urgency, no suspicious links, no brand impersonation, and no request for personal information or payment. The language is highly colloquial and conversational, suggesting it is from an acquaintance or friend.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01458", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The use of alarming language (\"PHONE COMPROMISED,\" \"extremely malicious files,\" \"IMMEDIATELY\") creates a sense of urgency designed to panic the recipient into acting without thinking. Furthermore, it contains a suspicious, non-standard URL (`hwqpzhm.com/QVdV9ppD`) which is characteristic of phishing attempts designed to trick users into clicking and entering personal information or downloading malware. The message attempts to impersonate a security alert, which is a common tactic in smishing.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01459", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS provides specific, directional instructions (\"Get down in gandhipuram and walk to cross cut road. Right side <> street road and turn at first right.\"). There are no indicators of urgency, requests for personal information, suspicious links, or brand impersonation. The message reads like a casual set of directions between acquaintances.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
