{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01511", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The message uses a generic greeting (\"User#63817\") rather than a personalized one, which is common in mass phishing attempts. More critically, it contains a suspicious, non-standard URL (`http://109.236.50.8/CST.php`). This IP-based, non-branded link is designed to trick the recipient into clicking, likely to steal credentials or install malware. The message also uses a vague \"good news\" hook, a common social engineering tactic to prompt immediate action.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01512", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. Key suspicious cues include:\n1. **Urgency:** The message creates a sense of urgency by stating the package \"cannot be delivered\" and demanding action \"within 12 hours.\"\n2. **Suspicious Link:** The provided URL, `https://uspssongshejj.top`, is highly suspicious. It does not use the official USPS domain (`usps.com`) and uses a generic, non-official top-level domain (.top), which is a common tactic in phishing.\n3. **Impersonation:** It impersonates a legitimate entity (USPS) to trick the recipient into clicking the link.\n4. **Request for Action/Information:** It pressures the user to click a link to \"confirm your address,\" which is a common method for harvesting personal information.\n\nThe combination of urgency, brand impersonation, and a clearly fraudulent link strongly classifies this as smishing.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
