{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01612", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message contains highly suggestive and unsolicited content (\"Your Wife will Love Your Boner\") combined with a suspicious, non-standard URL (\"laughramble.com/67YLUw\"). This combination strongly suggests a malicious or spam attempt, characteristic of smishing, even if the content itself is more suggestive spam than a typical financial phishing attempt. The unsolicited nature and the presence of a suspicious link are the key indicators.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01613", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It creates a sense of urgency (\"Your package delivery is on hold\") and demands immediate action (paying customs charges). Crucially, it directs the recipient to a suspicious link (`https://deutschepost-pack.net`). The domain name is a slight variation of a legitimate postal service, suggesting brand impersonation, which is a common tactic in phishing attacks. The request for payment via an unsolicited link is a major red flag.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
