{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01749", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. The message creates a sense of urgency (\"Your phone has been getting too many spam texts. Eradicate them now\"), which is a common tactic to prompt immediate action without critical thought. Furthermore, it directs the user to a suspicious, non-official-looking URL (`ex22r.com/wertABergA`). Legitimate service providers or carriers would typically not send unsolicited messages with such generic warnings and direct users to external, unknown links to \"eradicate\" spam.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
