{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01872", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The message uses a formal, urgent tone (\"For Security review, Due to unusual activity\") to create a sense of panic, which is a common social engineering tactic. It impersonates a legitimate financial institution (\"Bank of the West\"). Most critically, it directs the recipient to a shortened, suspicious URL (`https://tinyurl.com/2e2e85bw`) rather than a known, official bank website, which is a classic hallmark of phishing attempts designed to steal credentials or personal information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
