{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01874", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message appears to be a casual, personal communication between acquaintances. It uses informal language (\"u,\" \"sts,\" \"Call u\") and discusses a social plan (\"join me with sts later? Meeting them at five.\"). There are no indicators of urgency, suspicious links, brand impersonation, or requests for personal information or payment. Therefore, it is classified as legitimate.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01875", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several characteristics typical of smishing. The message uses promotional language (\"CONEXIÓN DIVINA YA ESTA DISPONIBLE/ DIME WITH CONEXIÓN DIVINA IS OUT NOW\") which is often used to lure recipients. More critically, it contains a shortened, suspicious URL (`https://llo.to/t/P9H03`). Shortened links are frequently employed in phishing attempts to obscure the true destination of the link, which is likely malicious. The message lacks any context or personalization, which is common in mass phishing campaigns.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01876", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message is very brief and lacks any typical indicators of smishing, such as urgent demands, suspicious links, requests for personal information, or brand impersonation. The content, \"Id onluy matters when getting on from offcampus,\" appears to be a casual, context-specific statement, possibly related to a university or organizational policy regarding identification when accessing resources remotely. The misspelling (\"onluy\") is minor and could be a typo rather than a deliberate phishing tactic.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01878", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It creates a sense of urgency (\"3 Malicious files have been found!\") and uses fear/threat to prompt immediate action. Crucially, it directs the recipient to a suspicious, shortened URL (`xsschju.com/W70A9956`) which is characteristic of phishing attempts designed to trick users into clicking and potentially installing malware or revealing credentials. The message impersonates a security feature notification, which is a common tactic in smishing attacks.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
