{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01914", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The use of an urgent tone (\"Your primary Funds Transfer account has been updated\") creates a sense of immediate need, pressuring the recipient to act quickly. More critically, the link provided, `https://safe-eddprocess3527.duckdns.org/`, is highly suspicious. It uses a non-standard, dynamically generated domain (`duckdns.org`) and includes random characters, which is characteristic of phishing attempts designed to mimic legitimate services. Furthermore, the message implies a security issue requiring immediate action via the provided link, which is a classic social engineering tactic used in smishing.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01915", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message contains several indicators of being non-malicious or \"ham.\" The language is informal, uses common internet abbreviations (\"FR'NDSHIP,\" \"V,\" \"r,\" \"nt,\" \"2,\" \"Evn,\" \"itz,\" \"4few,\" \"Bt,\" \"alwys,\" \"Gud,\" \"9t;-)\") and appears to be a personal, sentimental message rather than a transactional or urgent request. There are no suspicious links, requests for personal information, demands for payment, or attempts at brand impersonation. The content is conversational and benign.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
