{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-02037", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It creates a sense of urgency (\"Recover your account immediately\") by claiming the Amazon account has been locked due to failed login attempts. Crucially, it directs the recipient to a suspicious, non-official-looking URL (`http://s954071710.onlinehome.us/fixacs?logs`) to resolve the issue, which is a classic tactic used in phishing attacks to steal credentials.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
