{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00254", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The message uses brand impersonation (PayPal) to create a sense of legitimacy. It employs high urgency (\"Immediately\") to pressure the recipient into acting without thinking. Most critically, it contains a suspicious, shortened URL (`https://me2.do/GBIOwzEt?V4ZGKR`) which is characteristic of phishing attempts designed to redirect users to malicious sites. The message also implies an account issue, which is a common tactic in phishing scams to elicit a response or click.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00259", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It impersonates a government agency (IRS), which is a common tactic in phishing. It creates a sense of urgency (\"immediately,\" \"avoid potential delays or penalties,\" and a specific deadline) to pressure the recipient into acting without thinking. Furthermore, it requests \"accurate personal information,\" which is a classic red flag for phishing attempts designed to steal sensitive data. The promise of a tax refund is a common lure used by scammers.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
