{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00641", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The primary suspicious cues are the unsolicited nature of the message (a survey offer from a major retailer), the promise of a large reward ($100) which is a common lure in phishing attempts, and most critically, the suspicious URL (`http://moreshrill.shopping/PkRvik`). This URL does not appear to be an official Home Depot domain and uses a generic, suspicious-looking domain structure, suggesting it is designed to harvest credentials or personal information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
