{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01152", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several classic indicators of smishing. The primary suspicious cues are the urgent tone (\"Your delivery has been stopped\"), the inclusion of a tracking number (a common tactic to appear legitimate), and most significantly, the presence of a shortened, non-official-looking URL (`f94.us/VrVwq`). Legitimate delivery companies typically use their own domain names for tracking and resolution, not obscure, shortened links. The message attempts to create a sense of urgency to prompt immediate action, which is a hallmark of phishing attempts.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
