{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01439", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "ham", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message is very brief and lacks any immediate red flags typically associated with smishing, such as urgent threats, suspicious links, or requests for sensitive personal information or payment. The phrase \"Early bird! Any purchases yet?\" suggests a casual follow-up or a promotional nudge, which could be part of a legitimate marketing campaign or a conversation with a known contact. Without further context (like a sender ID or a link), the message appears benign.\n\nFINAL: ham"}
