{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01739", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several classic signs of a scam, classifying it as smishing. The primary suspicious cues are the unsolicited nature of the large financial offer (\"Grant of $1,450,000.00\"), which is a common lure in advance-fee fraud. Furthermore, the contact information provided is a generic, non-corporate Gmail address, which is highly suspicious for an official grant notification. The combination of an improbable, high-value offer and a non-official contact method strongly suggests an attempt to trick the recipient into engaging with a fraudulent scheme.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01740", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. It impersonates a legitimate entity (U.S.P.S.), creates a sense of urgency/problem (\"cannot be delivered due to incomplete address information\"), and directs the recipient to a suspicious, non-official-looking link (`https://axtras.cc`) to resolve the issue, which is a common tactic for harvesting personal information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
