{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01849", "condition": "clean", "attack_class": null, "seed": null, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. The primary red flag is the inclusion of a suspicious, shortened URL (`http://tonestrength.financial/7Mu7T15C`). The message attempts to create a sense of urgency (\"So you have to get it when you can\") tied to a perceived high-value offer (\"hardly ever give away 60$\") from a recognizable brand (Costco). While the initial context seems like a casual recommendation, the unsolicited link directing the user to an external, non-Costco domain is highly indicative of a phishing attempt designed to steal credentials or personal information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
