{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00029", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. The spelling and grammar are poor (\"Hezllo hich the site to download songs itts urgent pls\"), which is common in phishing attempts. The message creates a sense of urgency (\"itts urgent\") and directs the recipient to an external, unspecified \"site\" for a download, which is a classic tactic to trick users into clicking malicious links or downloading malware. The request is vague and lacks any legitimate context or branding.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
