{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00138", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The message uses leetspeak (\"W0W,\" \"$100,\" \"f0r,\" \"1-2\") which is often employed in phishing attempts to bypass basic filters or appear informal/urgent. It promises a large reward (\"$100\") for a very short task (\"1-2 Minute Walmart Servey\"), a common lure tactic. Most critically, it contains a suspicious, non-official-looking URL (`appliedtriumph.com/HW3SV3`) that is likely designed to harvest personal information or install malware, rather than directing to an official Walmart domain.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
