{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00508", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message consists only of a seemingly random string of characters followed by a domain name (`H1 poelacnewu33sdf.us`). There is no accompanying text, greeting, or context. The presence of a highly unusual, non-standard, and likely randomly generated domain name is a significant red flag. Such messages often serve as direct links to malicious phishing sites, making them highly suspicious.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
