{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00755", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message exhibits several suspicious cues indicative of smishing. The sender claims to be from \"Navy Federal Credit Union,\" which is a form of brand impersonation. The message states \"DE BIT LOCKED,\" creating a sense of urgency and alarm, a common tactic in phishing attempts. Furthermore, it provides a phone number to contact, which is a typical call-to-action in smishing scams, rather than a direct, secure link or a standard notification format. The use of \"Credi7 Union\" instead of the correct spelling (\"Credit Union\") is a subtle misspelling often used to evade spam filters.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
