{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00793", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several classic signs of smishing.\n1. **Suspicious Formatting/Typos:** The message contains numerous intentional misspellings and character substitutions (e.g., \"Th e,\" \"pack@ge,\" \"warehous3,\" \"deliviered,\" \"inform ation,\" \"Ple@se,\" \"addrpess,\" \"t he\") designed to bypass basic spam filters while mimicking a legitimate sender.\n2. **Urgency/Problem Creation:** It creates a sense of urgency by claiming a package delivery failure due to incomplete information.\n3. **Suspicious Link:** The URL provided, `https://uspsusa-us.com`, is highly suspicious. While it uses \"usps,\" the domain structure is not the official USPS domain and is designed to look similar (typosquatting).\n4. **Request for Action/Information:** It directs the user to click a link to \"confirm your address,\" which is a common tactic to steal personal information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
