{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-00867", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. The message uses an unusual, cryptic reference number (\"GD43 XVLL 18836\") and contains a notification about a transaction (\"De bit of $450 has ben made\"). The language is informal and contains typos (\"ben,\" \"d3tails\"), which is common in phishing attempts. Most critically, it includes a shortened, suspicious link (`https://bit.ly/3Nx3ar6`) that directs the recipient to \"look into details\" of the alleged transaction, a classic tactic used to trick users into clicking and revealing personal or financial information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
