{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01064", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message contains a seemingly benign greeting (\"Have a nie day\") followed immediately by a shortened, suspicious link (`https://shb52.app.link/K5KjPGI`). The link is not associated with any recognizable, legitimate brand, and the message itself lacks context, making the unsolicited link highly suspicious. Shortened, unknown links are a common tactic used in smishing attacks to direct users to malicious websites.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
