{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01068", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "ham", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS message exhibits several suspicious cues characteristic of smishing. The message uses unusual characters and substitutions (e.g., \"uBt\" for \"but,\" \"tran5fered\" for \"transferred\") which is a common tactic to bypass spam filters or appear informal/urgent. The content itself is vague and alarming (\"your brother transferred only...\"), creating a sense of urgency and prompting the recipient to seek clarification, which is a classic social engineering technique used in phishing. The use of symbols like `<#&gt;` and `+` without clear context further suggests a non-standard, potentially malicious communication. There is no clear, legitimate context provided.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
