{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01093", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The message uses an urgent tone (\"failed $57.78\") and references a specific, potentially unknown transaction or service (\"Eleven\"). Crucially, it includes a suspicious, non-standard link/call-to-action (\"U SE +18622898698 to reaqch us today\") which is designed to trick the recipient into contacting a fraudulent number or website to resolve the supposed issue, often leading to financial loss or data theft. The use of informal language and potential typos (\"y0u\", \"reaqch\") is also common in phishing attempts.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
