{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01123", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The message mimics a legitimate bank or financial alert (\"FRONT WAVE ALERT,\" \"debit TX successful\") to create a sense of urgency and alarm regarding a large, unexpected transaction ($689.00). The most significant red flag is the inclusion of a suspicious link (`https://onlinefrontwavedata.web.app`). This URL is not a standard, recognizable domain for a major financial institution and is designed to trick the recipient into clicking and entering sensitive information. The request to \"cancel\" the transaction via this link is a classic phishing tactic.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
