{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01136", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The SMS exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The message uses alarming language (\"Your Phone has been compromised!\") to create a sense of urgency and fear, a common tactic in phishing. Furthermore, it includes a suspicious, shortened URL (`pbizzz.com/J44rCi`) which is designed to trick the recipient into clicking a malicious link. The spelling and grammar errors (\"hkas,\" \"comprimised\") are also typical of hastily constructed phishing attempts.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
