{"model": "google/gemma-4-E4B-it", "template": "t3_neutral_explanation", "id": "msg-01176", "condition": "perturbed", "attack_class": "character", "seed": 0, "true_label": "smishing", "pred": "smishing", "parse_mode": "strict", "raw": "The message exhibits several strong indicators of smishing. The use of urgent language (\"Temporarily DISABLED\") creates a sense of panic, pressuring the recipient to act quickly. The link provided, \"http://myverifylink.cf,\" is highly suspicious; the domain extension (.cf) is often used in phishing attempts, and the URL structure is generic rather than belonging to a known, legitimate financial institution. Furthermore, the message implies an account issue (debit disabled) and directs the user to an external, unverified link to resolve it, which is a classic tactic used in phishing scams to steal credentials or personal information.\n\nFINAL: smishing"}
